  "name": "ANTI THROMBON - III  ACTIVITY FUNCTIONAL",
  "code": "1531",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The Anti-Thrombin III test serves for the rapid determination of the physiological activity of Anti-Thrombin III, and permits the diagnosis of hereditary and acquired Anti-Thromobin III deficiency which carry an elevated risk of Thrombosis. Acquired Anti Thrombin III deficiencies frequently occur as a consequence of consumption following large operations or disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC) in sepsis, nephrosis, liver parenchymal damage (hepatits, drug intoxication, alcoholism) and estrogen-containing contraceptives. The test enables early detection of patients with an elevated risk of thrombosis.</p>",
